@* REQ-UI-038 (BRD-90) — applies the stored theme to the document, once per window.

   Renders nothing. It exists as a component only because applying the theme needs JS interop, and
   interop is not available until after the first render — there is no earlier hook in a Blazor
   Hybrid head that can reach <html>.

   Mounted in Routes.razor rather than in a layout on purpose: the app has two layouts (MainLayout
   for the shell, AuthLayout for /login, /register and the first-run wizard), and a theme that only
   applied under one of them would leave the other rendering light on a dark install. Routes.razor
   wraps both. *@

@inject ThemeCoordinator Theme
@inject ILogger<ThemeInitializer> Logger

@code {
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            await Theme.EnsureAppliedAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // The document already carries whatever the first-paint shim in index.html put there,
            // so a failure here means "the theme may be stale", never "the app cannot render".
            Logger.LogWarning(ex, "Could not initialize the theme");
        }
    }
}
